							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "zW+xX1FmS1SME6NLcoM+Rw=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "Yes. The substantial duplication is the repeated construction of the bipartite paper–author Mondrian graph: adding nodes, adding each author-to-paper edge, and configuring the force layout occur in {{gtMethod:VSStudy>>#authorPaperGraphIn:}}, {{gtMethod:VSAuthor>>#authorPaperGraphIn:papers:authors:}}, {{gtMethod:VSPaperGroup>>#reachableAuthorPaperGraphIn:}}, and {{gtMethod:VSPaper>>#authorPaperGraphIn:papers:authors:startingPaper:connectStartingPaper:}}.\n\nThe proposed extraction keeps the distinct node styling and the paper-specific optional starting edges at their current call sites, while centralizing only the common topology/layout in {{gtMethod:VSPaperGroup>>#renderAuthorPaperGraphIn:papers:authors:nodeStencil:}}. Existing graph examples—especially {{gtMethod:VSStudyExamples>>#authorPaperGraph}}, {{gtMethod:VSStudyExamples>>#paperGroupReachableAuthorPaperGraph}}, {{gtMethod:VSAuthorExamples>>#reachableAuthorPaperGraph}}, and {{gtMethod:VSPaperExamples>>#reachableAuthorPaperGraph}}—should be run after applying these transformations."
						}
					]
